"medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Bryan Steil (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Bryan Steil seeks a fourth term in a southeastern Wisconsin district that leans slightly Republican but has become a top Democratic pickup target. Challenger Mitchell Berman, an ER nurse added to the DCCC's Red to Blue program, has kept the race close in recent surveys, though those polls come from Democratic-aligned sponsors. Steil holds an overwhelming financial advantage and has drawn support from a Trump-aligned super PAC.\n\nMost expert raters still call the race Lean or Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Steil roughly a two-in-three chance. The stock-trading issue has drawn negative coverage for Steil, and a favorable national environment keeps Democrats in range, but the incumbent's resources and the district's lean make him modestly favored.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.3311, "margin": -2.62}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3005, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3258, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3559, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2698, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2844, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2996, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3365, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3287, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3978, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3557, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4029, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.3963, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3263, "margin": -2.0}]}